# Cloudflare Pages redirects -- replaces netlify.toml's [[redirects]].
#
# Nothing left in here: Cloudflare Pages' _redirects only matches on PATH,
# not on Host -- a host-based rule (Netlify's own way of routing the 7
# client subdomains, and an earlier attempt at rewriting
# /.netlify/functions/* here too) silently never fires. Both are handled
# as real request-time logic instead: functions/_middleware.js does the
# subdomain routing, and every client-side call site was updated to call
# /api/<name> directly rather than depend on a path rewrite.
